{"decoder":"/root/anonymous_decoder70","reconstruction_fields":{"assumptions":"Only the initial binders are premises: finite-dimensional real inner-product/normed additive commutative structure on E; its measurable structure is Borel; V is twice continuously real Frechet differentiable; alpha,beta are nonnegative with alpha>0 and alpha<=beta; for all x,v, alpha||v||^2<=D^2V(x)[v,v]<=beta||v||^2; eta>0 and beta eta<=1. Derived measurable-space comparison and complete Hilbert structures are internal. Probability, the normalized kernel, all operators, root positivity and gap, inverse and identities are conclusions. In the final per-observable implication only integral f dJ=0 is an additional local premise; zero mean of g is concluded.","conclusion":"The full reconstruction in text enumerates every concluded conjunct. In particular: probability and conditional projection range/fixation; an every-state normalized conditional reflected kernel with equal marginals nu; the jointly produced pullback equivalence, selfadjoint isometric involution, selfadjoint Markov contraction and integral preservation; compression and adjoint-defect identities; positive commuting defect roots; produced constant vector and exact centered kernel; centered coercive positive unit with the same bounded two-sided selfadjoint inverse; centered selfadjoint commuting restriction A0 and square identity; B0=V0 GammaP0 with isometric V0 into ker P; all-H adjoint recovery through R and all-ker-P intertwining through D; and, for each centered f, the actual centered output g=U(Pf-(f-Pf)) with conditional/adjoint components satisfying the two block equations and exact pair squared-norm identity. No extra premise or RHS-only surrogate replaces any of these output components.","constant_dependencies":"alpha,beta are nonnegative and alpha>0, alpha<=beta; eta>0 and beta eta<=1. Exact reflection coefficient is 2, midpoint coefficient 1/2, Gaussian increment is sqrt(eta), and kernel penalty denominator is 8 eta. gamma=2 sqrt(alpha eta)/(1+alpha eta)>0; GammaP0-gamma I is positive and ||Inv||<=1/gamma. gamma and the explicit inverse bound use alpha,eta only; beta occurs in the input bounds and step-size condition. L^2 exponent is 2 and pair identities are exact squared-norm identities with coefficient 1. No further numerical dimension dependence is displayed. Common existential witnesses may depend on the full caller data and earlier witnesses; per-f components depend on f and those fixed witnesses.","domains":"E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product normed additive commutative group with Borel measurable structure. mu and nu are on E; J and Lambda on E x E. V:E->R; S is a Markov kernel E->E, with equality of S(y) for every y. H=L^2(J;R); K=L^2(nu;R); HP is the closed second-coordinate-measurable subspace of H; HP0=ker(<qP,->) within HP; Hperp=ker P within H. T,Gamma act on K; A,GammaP act on HP; B:HP->H; GammaP0,Inv,A0 act on HP0; B0,V0:HP0->Hperp; R:H->Hperp; D:Hperp->Hperp. B^*:H->HP, B0^*,V0^*:Hperp->HP0. All maps are real-linear with the displayed boundedness or isometric properties. Measures in the conclusions are probability measures, and L^2 elements are equivalence classes.","objects":"E; C^2 potential V; nonnegative alpha,beta and positive eta; volume, standard Gaussian, normalized tilted mu; joint pushforward J; nu=J.snd; reflected law Lambda and reflection F; H=L^2(J;R), K=L^2(nu;R), mY, HP and conditional-expectation operator P; pullback M; concluded kernel S, isometric equivalence e, reflection isometry U and Markov action T; compression A and residual B; positive defect root Gamma and transported GammaP; constant q, qP, exact centered subspace HP0, gamma, restricted root GammaP0, its inverse Inv and restricted A0; conditional complement Hperp=ker P, restricted residual B0, isometric embedding V0, residual map R and compression D; per-input fP,fperp,fV and actual output g with gP,gperp,gV.","quantifiers":"Caller data are arbitrary E with the displayed structures, V, alpha,beta,eta subject to the listed hypotheses; the Hessian bounds quantify every x,v in E. One nested existential chain jointly supplies S,e,U,T,Gamma,q,GammaP0,Inv,A0,B0,V0,R, in that order, before the final quantification over f. Each of these is a common witness for every later observable. Kernel fiber equality quantifies every y. P-fixation, A contraction and P B=0 quantify every HP element. U representative action quantifies every H observable; T action/contraction/integral preservation and q-pairing every K observable. Restriction, isometry and residual formulas quantify every element of their stated domains. B-adjoint recovery quantifies every g in all H; D representative action every h in Hperp; V0^*D=-A0 V0^* is an operator identity on all Hperp. The final implication quantifies every f in H with zero J-integral; only fP and gP are existential after that f, with the intermediate components defined as R f,V0^*R f,R g,V0^*R g.","scopes":"Measure equality S(y)=tilted volume holds for every y; the L^2 kernel formula is nu-AE separately per u; U g=g composed F is J-AE separately per g; q=1 is nu-AE. The positive lower bound, unit and bounded inverse hold only on HP0; GammaP qP=0 is on all HP. Hperp means zero P-conditional mean. V0 is an isometry into Hperp without an onto conclusion. B^* recovery holds on all H, and V0^*D=-A0V0^* on all Hperp, including vectors outside range V0. The last output construction is for every globally J-centered f; gP and gV are its real conditional and adjoint components, not symbols defined by the block RHS. No common AE exceptional set across observables, full-HP inverse, full-Hperp spanning, final contraction rate, or source-fidelity verdict is asserted."},"slot_decisions":[{"decision":"All and only the initial binders are assumptions; nonnegative scalar types, positivity, ordering, C^2, uniform two-sided Hessian bounds and beta eta<=1 are retained.","slot":"caller-boundary"},{"decision":"Real finite-dimensional Borel inner-product E; volume tilting, Gaussian product pushforward, second marginal and reflected pushforward are distinct exact measures.","slot":"base-space-and-measures"},{"decision":"HP is the second-coordinate measurable closed subspace; P is conditional expectation included in H. Its range and fixation are genuine conclusions.","slot":"projection-structure"},{"decision":"S,e,U,T,Gamma,q,GammaP0,Inv,A0,B0,V0,R are common produced data; none is an additional public premise or chosen per final f.","slot":"common-existential-chain"},{"decision":"Every-state exact normalized tilt with midpoint (y+x)/2 and penalty ||y-x||^2/(8 eta); Lambda conditional law and both nu marginals are concluded.","slot":"kernel-fibers"},{"decision":"e is an onto isometric linear equivalence K->HP with inclusion equal to M; distinguish it from the later possibly nononto V0.","slot":"pullback-equivalence"},{"decision":"U is isometric, involutive and selfadjoint; U g=g composed F J-AE per g, on all H.","slot":"reflection-action"},{"decision":"T is selfadjoint bounded contraction on all K; per-u nu-AE kernel action and exact integral preservation are separate conjuncts.","slot":"markov-action"},{"decision":"A=e T e^-1 and compressed U; B=(I-P) U P inclusion, P B=0; operator domains HP and H are kept distinct.","slot":"compression-and-leakage"},{"decision":"Gamma and GammaP are positive commuting roots; B^*B=GammaP^2 is on HP; no inversion of GammaP on HP.","slot":"defect-root"},{"decision":"q=1 AE, Tq=q and pairing with integral are produced. HP0 is exactly the qP-orthogonal kernel, equivalent to zero marginal mean.","slot":"constant-and-centering"},{"decision":"gamma is exact; positive lower bound, unit and same two-sided selfadjoint inverse with norm<=1/gamma are only on HP0.","slot":"gap-and-inverse"},{"decision":"A0 is an actual restriction of A, selfadjoint, commutes with the same GammaP0 and Inv, with A0^2+GammaP0^2=I.","slot":"centered-A-restriction"},{"decision":"Hperp=ker P is stronger than a bare total-zero-mean label; inherited completeness is internal.","slot":"conditional-complement"},{"decision":"B0 restricts B; V0=B0 Inv and B0=V0 GammaP0; V0^*V0=I and norm preservation assert an embedding, no reverse-product or onto identity.","slot":"polar-embedding"},{"decision":"R lands in Hperp with ambient Rg=g-Pg; B^*g=inclusion(B0^*Rg) holds for every ambient g.","slot":"ambient-adjoint-recovery"},{"decision":"D=R U inclusion; its coerced H-valued operator formula is on all Hperp, as is V0^*D=-A0V0^*.","slot":"residual-compression"},{"decision":"For each J-centered f, fP is produced by conditional expectation; fperp=Rf and fV=V0^*fperp. Retain both adjoint/coercion identities, full Pythagoras and the fV norm bound.","slot":"input-component-production"},{"decision":"g is exactly U(Pf-(f-Pf)); its zero mean is concluded. gP is produced as conditional expectation of this g, gperp=Rg and gV=V0^*gperp.","slot":"actual-output-production"},{"decision":"gP=A0fP-GammaP0fV and gV=GammaP0fP+A0fV assert the identities of actual output components; RHS does not merely define them. Pair squared norm is exactly preserved.","slot":"output-block-identities"},{"decision":"Each observable has its own AE equality; no simultaneous pointwise version or universal common null set is inferred.","slot":"AE-scope"},{"decision":"Retain 2,1/2,8, exponent 2, gamma formula and inverse bound; beta enters assumptions; no extra dimension or higher-derivative constant is introduced.","slot":"constants"},{"decision":"No source identity/text/anchor, fidelity verdict, proof, compilation check, final convergence/contraction rate, V0 onto property or all-HP root inverse is inferred.","slot":"unresolved-boundary"}],"visibility":{"source_identity_visible":false,"source_text_visible":false}}